NNAAMMEE
     nneewwaalliiaasseess — rebuild mail aliases

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nneewwaalliiaasseess [--ff _f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The nneewwaalliiaasseess utility makes changes to the mail aliases file visible to
     smtpd(8).  It should be run every time the aliases(5) file is changed.
     The location of the alias file is defined in smtpd.conf(5), and defaults
     to _/_e_t_c_/_m_a_i_l_/_a_l_i_a_s_e_s.

     The options are as follows:

     --ff _f_i_l_e
             Use _f_i_l_e as the configuration file, instead of the default
             _/_e_t_c_/_m_a_i_l_/_s_m_t_p_d_._c_o_n_f.

     If using database (db) files, nneewwaalliiaasseess is equivalent to running
     makemap(8) as follows:

           # makemap -t aliases /etc/mail/aliases

     If using plain text files, nneewwaalliiaasseess is equivalent to running smtpctl(8)
     as follows:

           # smtpctl update table aliases

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/mail/aliases     List of local user mail aliases.
     /etc/mail/virtual     List of virtual host aliases.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The nneewwaalliiaasseess utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     smtpd.conf(5), makemap(8), smtpctl(8), smtpd(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The nneewwaalliiaasseess command first appeared in OpenBSD 4.6 as a replacement for
     the equivalent command shipped with sendmail.

